  <static seed="1970" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/Percent/MTH20PercentOfNumberType1_30.pg">
    <statement><p><m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m> is <fillin characters="7" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>770</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 1</p>
<p>We will use proportion to solve this problem. Assume <m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m> is <m>x</m>, so <lq/><m>350</m> out of <m>100</m><rq/> corresponds to <lq/><m>x</m> out of <m>220</m><rq/>.</p>
<p>We will write and solve the proportion:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \frac{350}{100} \amp = \frac{x}{220} \\
   100x \amp = 350 \cdot 220 \\
   100x \amp = 77000 \\
   \frac{100x}{100} \amp = \frac{77000}{100} \\
   x \amp = 770
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p><m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m> is <m>770</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 2</p>
<p>We will use the percentage formula to solve this problem. This translation from English to math may help you remember the percentage formula.</p>
<p><m>2 \text{ is } 50\% \text{ of } 4 \iff 2 = 0.5 \cdot 4</m></p>
<p>The question is: What is <m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m>? Assume <m>x</m> is <m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m>. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
    \begin{aligned}
        x  \amp  = 3.5 \cdot 220 \\
        \amp  = 770 
        \end{aligned}
        }</m></p>
<p><m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m> is <m>770</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 3</p>
<p>In the sentence <lq/><m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m> is what,<rq/></p>
<p><ul label="disc">
<li>
<p><lq/>what<rq/> is the <alert>percentage</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>350\%</m> is the <alert>rate</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>220</m> is the <alert>base</alert> (following the word <lq/>of<rq/>).</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>By the formula <m>\text{percentage} = \text{rate} \cdot \text{base}</m>, we do a multiplication to solve the problem:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{percentage } = \text{rate} \cdot \text{base} = 350\% \cdot 220 = 3.5 \cdot 220 = 770 }</m></p>
<p><m>350\%</m> of <m>220</m> is <m>770</m>.</p>
</solution>
